⍝ type variables (§9.4): each call fixes α, β from its arguments, and the function is
checked and compiled once per instance ⍝
⦃ ⦄ ⟨ α ⊸ α ⟩ ᚡᚠ ⸫
⸫ ᚡᚢ ⟨ α β ⊸ β α ⟩ ⦃ ⧗⁰ ⧗¹ ⧖ ⧖ ⦄
⍝ ᚡᚤ a i: element i of an array of any classical type
⸫ ᚡᚤ ⟨ ◌α ⊸ ℤ ⟦ α ⟧ ⟗ ⟩ ⦃ ⌖̱ ⦄
⍝ ᚡᚥ a b: the larger of two values of the same type
⸫ ᚡᚥ ⟨ α ⊸ α α ⟩ ⦃ ⦃ ⧗⁰ ⌁ ⧖ ⦄ ⁼ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⋔ ≶ ⧗¹ ⧗⁰ ⧗¹ ⧗⁰ ⧖ ⧖ ⦄
⍝ ᚡᚦ x: x and a copy, through ᚡᚠ: one generic calls another
⸫ ᚡᚦ ⟨ α α ⊸ α ⟩ ⦃ ᚡᚠ ⧗⁰ ᚡᚠ ⧗⁰ ⧖ ⦄
⍝ ᚡᚧ x n: x·x·…·x (n factors), recursively, for ℤ or ℝ
⸫ ᚡᚧ ⟨ α ⊸ ℤ α ⟩ ⦃ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⊠ ᚡᚧ ⊟ △ ⧗¹ ⧗⁰ ⧗⁰ ⧖ ⧖ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⋔ ≶ △ ⧗¹ ⧗¹ ⧗⁰ ⧖ ⧖ ⦄
⍝ ᚡᚨ a b: charges stay with the variable
⸫ ᚡᚨ ⟨ α⁽ᵘ⁾ ⊸ α⁽ᵘ⁾ α⁽ᵘ⁾ ⟩ ⦃ ⊞ ⦄
⦃
  ⎙ ᚡᚠ ⊕ ⎙ ᚡᚠ △▽△
  ○△ ⊖ ᚡᚢ ⎙ ⎙
  ⌁̵ ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ ⎙ ⦄ ⁇ ᚡᚤ △ ⟗ ⟦ ○△○△ ▽△▽△ △○△ ⟧
  △△ ○○△ ᚡᚥ ⎙ ⊖ ⊕ ᚡᚥ ⎙
  ⎙ ⊠ ᚡᚦ ▽▽△
  ○△ △△ ᚡᚧ ⎙
  the same functions for ℝ: new instances ⍝
  △⁝△ ▽△ ᚡᚧ ⎙ △⁝△ ▽△⁝○ ᚡᚥ ⎙
